    pr_ref:  # bae0
    description: "Found by the 0006 adversarial refutation pass.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: collapsed_flow_count IS the row-level denominator. Every per-row precision figure the project has published is computed through it. 0006 reports row precision (31.5%) beside situation precision (33.9%) because the ratified frame makes SITUATION canonical; this item is a second, independent reason that was the right call, and it means the row figure is the less trustworthy of the two.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED: the direction and magnitude of the bias. Two refuters found totals too HIGH and one found totals both high and low against a single rule, so this is not yet demonstrated to be uniform inflation. The intended collapse key is not documented anywhere the refuters could find, so none of them could state the rule they were checking against -- that is itself part of the defect."  # bae0
    fields:  # bae0
      statement: "collapsed_flow_count (the situation -> raw-pair multiplier, INV-karud) cannot be reconciled against the source/sink call sites that exist in the repository, and is inflated in at least one direction. Three independent refuters on three repositories: kamaraflow#4 reports 8 where the repo holds exactly ONE os.makedirs site and TWO argv read sites; shellcheck#3 reports 4 where at most 2 (newIORef site x modifyIORef site) exist in the anchoring module, the extra 2 matching a cross-module product whose pairs act on refs created by their own modules and therefore carry no value; ArkLib totals fit no single counting rule within one repository (#4=2 for 2 sources x 1 sink, but #0 and #6 report 1 for the same 2x1 shape, while #1 reports 1 against EIGHT write sites and #3 reports 6 against 4 open sites)."  # bae0
      root_cause: "The situation->pair collapse key is undocumented and appears to form a cross product over source and sink sites without checking that a given pair carries a value."  # bae0
- op: discuss  # 45fb
  at: '2026-08-27T21:32:34Z'  # 45fb
  by: agent  # 45fb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 45fb
  clock: 2  # 45fb
  nonce: 45fb  # 45fb
  message: "REPRODUCED ON ALL THREE NAMED REPOS, and the rule is now identified. The\nstatement's first clause holds; its second clause (\"inflated in at least one\ndirection\") is NOT established and, on the evidence below, is probably wrong.\n\nTHE ACTUAL RULE. collapsed_flow_count is the number of\n(SOURCE CALL SITE, SINK CALL SITE) pairs where the sink site is REACHABLE from\nthe source site's caller in the call graph -- `sink_node in reachable` at\ntaint.py:2477. It is NOT a count of value flows, and it is NOT the product of\nthe distinct primitive NAMES the record prints.\n\nLIVE REPRO, shipped CLI, fresh XDG_CACHE_HOME per repo, claim\n{taint_flow: {source_taint: host_secret, prohibited_sink_zone: host_fs}}:\n\n  kamaraflow  collapsed=8   source_primitives = [parse_args, sys.argv]        (2)\n                            sink_primitives   = [open, file.write,\n                                                 os.makedirs, shutil.copyfile] (4)\n              2 x 4 = 8. The refuter counted os.makedirs sites (correctly ONE)\n              and did not see that three other sinks share the collapsed group\n              -- sink_symbol is NOT in the collapse key, only sink_zone is.\n\n  shellcheck  collapsed=2 with ONE source primitive and ONE sink primitive, so\n              the product rule visibly fails. Traced to the edges:\n                striptests nodes reading env       : 1  (the file node)\n                striptests nodes calling redirect.>: 2  (the file node, and\n                                                        `sponge`, reachable\n                                                        from it)\n              1 source site x 2 reachable sink sites = 2. Exactly the count.\n\n  ArkLib      collapsed=6 with 1 source primitive and 3 sink primitives\n              (1x3=3). Same cause: site multiplicity, not name multiplicity.\n              This is the \"fits no single counting rule\" report -- there IS a\n              single rule, it is just not a rule over the names the record\n              shows.\n\nWHY NO REFUTER COULD RECONCILE IT, stated precisely because the item asks for\nit. The record emits collapsed_flow_count together with the DISTINCT PRIMITIVE\nNAMES (source_primitives / sink_primitives) and nothing about site\nmultiplicity. Two rows with identical source_primitives and sink_primitives\nlegitimately carry different counts -- shellcheck has three rows at 1x1 -> 1 and\none at 1x1 -> 2 -- and nothing in the record distinguishes them. The number is\nreconcilable ONLY against the call graph's reachable set, which the record does\nnot carry. That is the defect.\n\nNOT DOUBLE-COUNTING. Every pair traced corresponds to a distinct (source edge,\nsink edge) with a real reachability path. source_callers is built one entry per\nEDGE, and edges are deduplicated on (src, dst, edge_type) (INV-vukiv), so the\nsame site cannot enter twice. I found no arithmetic inflation. The refuters'\ncounts were low because they counted primitive OCCURRENCES in source text;\nthe tool counts reachable SITE PAIRS.\n\nTHE SUBSTANTIVE PROBLEM IS NOT THE ARITHMETIC, IT IS WHAT THE NUMBER MEANS.\nFor analysis_method=structural the pair test is pure call-graph reachability\nwith NO check that a value crosses -- which is what \"structural\" and\nconfidence=\"approximate\" mean under ADR-0017, so it is not a bug in the\npropagator. But this count is the ROW-LEVEL PRECISION DENOMINATOR. Precision\ncomputed over it is therefore a rate over REACHABILITY PAIRS, not over claims\nthat a value flowed. A file-anchored source node (kamaraflow's source_symbol is\n`train_script.py:1-1:file:file`) reaches everything the file calls, so the\nmultiplier grows with file size rather than with anything about taint.\n\nThis is an independent, mechanical reason 0006 was right to make SITUATION\ncanonical, and it is stronger than \"the row figure is less trustworthy\": the\nrow figure is a rate over a different population than the one the claim is\nabout.\n\nALSO NOTE, against the item's root_cause: the collapse KEY is documented, in\n_collapse_to_situations' own docstring (\"WHAT IS IN THE KEY, AND WHY EACH\",\ntaint.py:~605). What is undocumented is the MULTIPLIER -- what len(grp) counts\n-- and that is what no refuter could find."  # 45fb
